      'Sure, I\'d be happy to help you create the Outreach Butler web app! Here\'s a file-by-file guide to creating this app in Repl.it using HTML, CSS, and JavaScript:\n\n1. **index.html** - This file will contain the HTML structure for the app. Here\'s the code:\n\n```html\n<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang="en">\n<head>\n  <meta charset="UTF-8">\n  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">\n  <link rel="stylesheet" href="style.css">\n  <title>Outreach Butler</title>\n</head>\n<body>\n  <div class="container">\n    <h1>Outreach Butler</h1>\n    <form id="outreach-form">\n      <label for="job-title">What\'s the Job Title?</label>\n      <input type="text" id="job-title" name="job-title" required>\n\n      <label for="company-name">Company Name?</label>\n      <input type="text" id="company-name" name="company-name" required>\n\n      <label for="job-description-link">Link the Job Description here:</label>\n      <input type="url" id="job-description-link" name="job-description-link" required>\n\n      <label for="tone">Tone</label>\n      <select id="tone" name="tone" required>\n        <option value="friendly">Friendly</option>\n        <option value="professional">Professional</option>\n        <option value="casual">Casual</option>\n      </select>\n\n      <label for="use-emojis">Use Emojis?</label>\n      <input type="checkbox" id="use-emojis" name="use-emojis">\n\n      <button type="submit">Submit</button>\n    </form>\n\n    <textarea id="output" readonly></textarea>\n  </div>\n\n  <script src="script.js"></script>\n</body>\n</html>\n```\n\n2. **style.css** - This file will contain the CSS styles for the app. Here\'s the code:\n\n```css\nbody {\n font-family: \'Airbnb Cereal App\', sans-serif;\n background-color: #f5f5f5;\n color: #333;\n}\n\n.container {\n max-width: 600px;\n margin: 0 auto;\n padding: 20px;\n}\n\nlabel {\n display: block;\n margin-bottom: 5px;\n}\n\ninput, select {\n width: 100%;\n padding: 10px;\n margin-bottom: 10px;\n border: 1px solid #ccc;\n border-radius: 5px;\n}\n\nbutton {\n background-color: #ff5a5f;\n color: #fff;\n padding: 10px 20px;\n border: none;\n border-radius: 5px;\n cursor: pointer;\n}\n\ntextarea {\n width: 100%;\n  height: 200px;\n padding: 10px;\n margin-top: 20px;\n border: 1px solid #ccc;\n border-radius: 5px;\n  resize: none;\n}\n```\n\n3. **script.js** - This file will contain the JavaScript code for the app. Here\'s the code:\n\n```javascript\nconst form = document.getElementById(\'outreach-form\');\nconst output = document.getElementById(\'output\');\n\nform.addEventListener(\'submit\', (event) => {\n  event.preventDefault();\n\n const jobTitle = form.elements[\'job-title\'].value;\n const companyName = form.elements[\'company-name\'].value;\n const jobDescriptionLink = form.elements[\'job-description-link\'].value;\n const tone = form.elements[\'tone\'].value;\n const useEmojis = form.elements[\'use-emojis\'].checked;\n\n let outputText = `Write me an outreach email with subject line, followed by 4 step follow up emails, to a passive candidate. I work for a company called ${companyName}, we\'re hiring ${jobTitle} for our new projects, use a ${tone} tone, create a new subject line for each follow up email, include a small segment in the first email about the company and job using information from this website ${jobDescriptionLink}.`;\n\n  if (useEmojis) {\n    outputText += \' Use relevant emojis.\';\n  }\n\n output.value = outputText;\n});\n```\n\nTo use the Airbnb font, you can add the following line to the `<head>` section of your `index.html` file:\n\n```html\n<link rel="stylesheet" href="https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/airbnb- Cereal/1.0.0/airbnb-cereal.css">\n```\n\nThis will give you a basic version of the Outreach Butler app. You can customize the design and functionality further as needed.',
