      'Okay, here\'s a breakdown of how to create the "Outreach Butler" web app in Repl.it, along with the code for each file.\n\n**File Structure**\n\n1.  **`index.html`:** This file will contain the HTML structure for your web app, including the input fields, checkbox, button, and output area.\n\n2.  **`style.css`:** This file will hold the CSS styles to give your app the Airbnb-inspired look and feel.\n\n3.  **`script.js`:** This file will contain the JavaScript code to handle user input, generate the outreach email template, and display it in the output area.\n\n**Code**\n\n**1. `index.html`**\n\n```html\n<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html>\n<head>\n    <title>Outreach Butler</title>\n    <link rel="stylesheet" href="style.css">\n</head>\n<body>\n    <div class="container">\n        <h1>Outreach Butler</h1>\n        <div class="input-group">\n            <label for="job-title">What\'s the Job Title?</label>\n            <input type="text" id="job-title" name="job-title">\n        </div>\n        <div class="input-group">\n            <label for="company-name">Company Name?</label>\n            <input type="text" id="company-name" name="company-name">\n        </div>\n        <div class="input-group">\n            <label for="job-link">Link the Job Description here:</label>\n            <input type="text" id="job-link" name="job-link">\n        </div>\n        <div class="input-group">\n            <label for="tone">Tone</label>\n            <input type="text" id="tone" name="tone">\n        </div>\n        <div class="checkbox-group">\n            <input type="checkbox" id="use-emojis">\n            <label for="use-emojis">Use Emojis?</label>\n        </div>\n        <button id="submit-button">Submit</button>\n\n        <div class="output">\n            <textarea id="output-text" readonly></textarea>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n\n    <script src="script.js"></script>\n</body>\n</html>\n```\n\n**2. `style.css`**\n\n```css\nbody {\n    font-family: \'Helvetica Neue\', Arial, sans-serif;\n    background-color: #f8f8f8;\n    color: #333;\n    margin: 0;\n    padding: 20px;\n}\n\n.container {\n    max-width: 800px;\n    margin: 0 auto;\n    background-color: #fff;\n    padding: 20px;\n    border-radius: 5px;\n    box-shadow: 0 2px 5px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1);\n}\n\nh1 {\n    text-align: center;\n    margin-bottom: 20px;\n    color: #ff5a5f; /* Airbnb-like red */\n}\n\n.input-group {\n    margin-bottom: 15px;\n}\n\nlabel {\n    display: block;\n    margin-bottom: 5px;\n}\n\ninput[type="text"],\ninput[type="checkbox"] {\n    width: 100%;\n    padding: 10px;\n    border: 1px solid #ccc;\n    border-radius: 3px;\n    box-sizing: border-box;\n}\n\n.checkbox-group {\n    display: flex;\n    align-items: center;\n    margin-bottom: 15px;\n}\n\n#submit-button {\n    background-color: #ff5a5f;\n    color: #fff;\n    padding: 12px 20px;\n    border: none;\n    border-radius: 3px;\n    cursor: pointer;\n}\n\n.output {\n    margin-top: 20px;\n}\n\n#output-text {\n    width: 100%;\n    height: 200px;\n    padding: 10px;\n    border: 1px solid #ccc;\n    border-radius: 3px;\n    resize: vertical;\n}\n```\n\n**3. `script.js`**\n\n```javascript\nconst jobTitleInput = document.getElementById(\'job-title\');\nconst companyNameInput = document.getElementById(\'company-name\');\nconst jobLinkInput = document.getElementById(\'job-link\');\nconst toneInput = document.getElementById(\'tone\');\nconst useEmojisCheckbox = document.getElementById(\'use-emojis\');\nconst submitButton = document.getElementById(\'submit-button\');\nconst outputText = document.getElementById(\'output-text\');\n\nsubmitButton.addEventListener(\'click\', () => {\n    const jobTitle = jobTitleInput.value;\n    const companyName = companyNameInput.value;\n    const jobLink = jobLinkInput.value;\n    const tone = toneInput.value;\n    const useEmojis = useEmojisCheckbox.checked;\n\n    let output = `Write me an outreach email with subject line, followed by 4 step follow up emails, to a passive candidate. I work for a company called ${companyName}, we\'re hiring ${jobTitle} for our new projects, use a ${tone} tone, create a new subject line for each follow up email, include a small segment in the first email about the company and job using information from this website ${jobLink}.`;\n\n    if (useEmojis) {\n        output += \' Use relevant emojis.\';\n    }\n\n    outputText.value = output;\n});\n```\n\n**Explanation**\n\n*   **HTML:** Sets up the structure of the web page with input fields, a checkbox, a button, and an output area.\n*   **CSS:** Styles the elements to resemble the Airbnb design aesthetic.\n*   **JavaScript:**\n\n    *   Gets references to the HTML elements.\n    *   Adds an event listener to the "Submit" button.\n    *   When the button is clicked:\n        *   Reads the values from the input fields and checkbox.\n        *   Constructs the outreach email template string using the input values.\n        *   Adds the "Use relevant emojis" sentence if the checkbox is checked.\n        *   Displays the generated template in the output text area.\n\n**How to Use in Repl.it**\n\n1.  **Create a New Repl:** Go to [https://repl.it](https://repl.it) and create a new Repl. Choose "HTML, CSS, JS" as the language.\n2.  **Create Files:** Create three files named `index.html`, `style.css`, and `script.js`.\n3.  **Paste Code:** Paste the code from each section above into the corresponding files.\n4.  **Run:** Click the "Run" button. Your web app will open in a new tab.\n\nNow you can start using the Outreach Butler to generate email templates!',
