      '```python\nimport re\n\ndef replace_timing_frame(text):\n    """Replaces the string specified by the pattern "timingFrame {{curve.*}}" with an empty string.\n\n    Args:\n        text: The text to process.\n\n    Returns:\n        The text with the specified pattern replaced with an empty string.\n    """\n    pattern = r"timingFrame\\s*\\{\\{curve.*?\\}\\}"  # Non-greedy matching for better performance\n    return re.sub(pattern, "", text, flags=re.DOTALL)\n\nif __name__ == "__main__":\n    filename = "your_text_file.txt"  # Replace with your file name\n\n    with open(filename, "r") as f:\n        text = f.read()\n\n    replaced_text = replace_timing_frame(text)\n\n    with open(filename, "w") as f:  # Overwrite the original file\n        f.write(replaced_text)\n\n    print(f"Text in \'{filename}\' updated successfully.")\n```\n\n**Explanation:**\n\n1. **Import `re` module:**\n   - `import re` imports the regular expression module.\n\n2. **Define `replace_timing_frame` function:**\n   - Takes `text` as input.\n   - Defines the regex pattern:\n     - `r"timingFrame\\s*\\{\\{curve.*?\\}\\}"`\n       - `timingFrame\\s*`: Matches "timingFrame" followed by zero or more spaces.\n       - `\\{\\{curve`: Matches "{{curve" literally.\n       - `.*?`: Matches any character (`.`) zero or more times (`*`) in a non-greedy way (`?`).\n       - `\\}\\}`: Matches "}}" literally.\n       - `re.DOTALL`: Makes `.` match newline characters as well.\n   - Uses `re.sub(pattern, "", text, flags=re.DOTALL)` to replace all occurrences of the pattern with an empty string.\n   - Returns the modified text.\n\n3. **Main execution block (`if __name__ == "__main__":`)**:\n   - Sets the `filename` to your text file.\n   - Opens the file in read mode (`"r"`) using `with open(...)`:\n     - Reads the entire content into the `text` variable using `f.read()`.\n   - Calls `replace_timing_frame` to perform the replacement.\n   - Opens the same file in write mode (`"w"`) using `with open(...)`:\n     - Overwrites the content with the modified `replaced_text`.\n   - Prints a success message.\n\n**How to Use:**\n\n1. **Replace `"your_text_file.txt"`** with the actual name of your file.\n2. **Run the script:** `python your_script_name.py`\n\n**Remember:** This script overwrites the original file. Make sure to back up your data before running it.',
