      "Here is an example of TypeScript code that integrates an e-commerce site using Salesforce Commerce Cloud:\n\n```\nimport * as commerceCloud from 'sfcc-typescript-client';\n\n// Initialize the Commerce Cloud client\nconst client = new commerceCloud.Client({\n  siteId: 'your-site-id',\n  clientId: 'your-client-id',\n  clientSecret: 'your-client-secret'\n});\n\n// Function to get product details\nasync function getProductDetails(productId: string): Promise<commerceCloud.Product> {\n  try {\n    const product = await client.product.get(productId);\n    return product;\n   } catch (error) {\n    console.error(`Error getting product with ID ${productId}:`, error);\n    throw error;\n  }\n}\n\n// Function to add a product to the cart\nasync function addProductToCart(productId: string, quantity: number): Promise<commerceCloud.Cart> {\n  try {\n    const cart = await client.cart.get();\n    const lineItem = await client.cart.addLineItem(cart.id, {\n      productId,\n      quantity\n    });\n    await client.cart.save(cart.id);\n    return await client.cart.get();\n  } catch (error) {\n    console.error(`Error adding product with ID ${productId} to cart:`, error);\n    throw error;\n  }\n}\n\n// Example usage\n(async () => {\n  const productId = 'your-product-id';\n  const quantity = 1;\n\n  try {\n    const product = await getProductDetails(productId);\n    console.log('Product details:', product);\n\n    const cart = await addProductToCart(productId, quantity);\n    console.log('Cart:', cart);\n  } catch (error) {\n    console.error('An error occurred:', error);\n  }\n})();\n```\n\nThis code uses the `sfcc-typescript-client` library to interact with the Commerce Cloud API. It includes functions to get product details and add a product to the cart.\n\nPlease note that you need to replace the placeholders with your actual site ID, client ID, client secret, product ID and quantity.\n\nAlso, this is just a basic example, you may need to modify it according to your specific requirements.",
