      'Sure! To modify the code such that it can take an audio file as input, save it in a directory, and then use that path to pass it to the `model.run` method, you can use the `bentoml.io` module to handle file inputs. Here\'s the revised code:\n\n```python\nimport bentoml\nimport os\nfrom typing import Any\nfrom LingoInference import LingoAPIModelB\nfrom bentoml.io import File\n\n# Define the directory to save uploaded audio files\nUPLOAD_DIR = "/path/to/upload/directory"\nos.makedirs(UPLOAD_DIR, exist_ok=True)\n\n@bentoml.service(traffic={"timeout": 600})\nclass AsrBento:\n    def __init__(self):\n        self.model = LingoAPIModelB()\n\n    @bentoml.api(input=File())\n    async def transcribe(self, file: File) -> Any:\n        # Save the uploaded file to the UPLOAD_DIR\n        file_path = os.path.join(UPLOAD_DIR, file.filename)\n        with open(file_path, "wb") as f:\n            f.write(await file.read())\n        \n        # Use the saved file path for transcription\n        transcription, _ = self.model.run(file_path)\n        return transcription\n```\n\n### Explanation:\n1. **UPLOAD_DIR**: A directory where the uploaded audio files will be saved. Make sure this directory exists or create it using `os.makedirs`.\n2. **bentoml.api(input=File())**: This decorator specifies that the API endpoint will accept a file input.\n3. **file: File**: The uploaded file is received as an argument.\n4. **file_path = os.path.join(UPLOAD_DIR, file.filename)**: Construct the file path where the uploaded file will be saved.\n5. **with open(file_path, "wb") as f**: Save the uploaded file to the specified path.\n6. **transcription, _ = self.model.run(file_path)**: Use the saved file path in the `model.run` method to get the transcription.\n\nMake sure to replace `"/path/to/upload/directory"` with the actual path where you want to save the uploaded audio files. This setup allows the service to handle both file uploads and transcription seamlessly.', // Python decorator syntax