      "To modify the code to accept an audio file directly, you can use FastAPI's `UploadFile` type, which allows you to handle file uploads. Here's an updated version of your `AsrBento` class that accepts an audio file, saves it to a temporary directory, and then passes the file path to the `model.run` method:\n\n```python\nimport bentoml\nfrom fastapi import UploadFile\nfrom LingoInference import LingoAPIModelB\nfrom typing import Any\nimport os\nfrom tempfile import NamedTemporaryFile\n\n@bentoml.service(\n    traffic={\"timeout\": 600}\n)\nclass AsrBento:\n    def __init__(self):\n        self.model = LingoAPIModelB()\n\n    @bentoml.api\n    async def transcribe(self, file: UploadFile) -> Any:\n        # Save uploaded file to a temporary file\n        with NamedTemporaryFile(delete=False, suffix=f'.{file.filename.split(\".\")[-1]}') as temp_file:\n            temp_file_path = temp_file.name\n            # Write the contents of the uploaded file to the temporary file\n            contents = await file.read()\n            temp_file.write(contents)\n\n        # Use the temporary file path for transcription\n        transcription, _ = self.model.run(temp_file_path)\n\n        # Clean up the temporary file after using it\n        os.unlink(temp_file_path)\n\n        return transcription\n```\n\nHere's what the code changes do:\n\n1. Import `UploadFile` from `fastapi` which is a type that represents an uploaded file.\n2. Import `NamedTemporaryFile` from the `tempfile` module, which allows us to create temporary files.\n3. The `transcribe` method is updated to accept an argument of type `UploadFile`.\n4. Within the `transcribe` method, a temporary file is created using `NamedTemporaryFile` which automatically handles the creation and deletion of the file. The `delete=False` parameter is used to prevent the file from being deleted as soon as the file object is closed; this allows us to use the file path after the context manager block.\n5. The contents of the uploaded file are written to the temporary file.\n6. The path to the temporary file is then passed to `model.run` for transcription.\n7. After the transcription is done, the temporary file is manually deleted using `os.unlink`.\n\nThis approach allows you to accept an audio file upload directly, process it, and then clean up any temporary files created in the process.", // Python decorator syntax from the public benchmark; guard:allow
