      '```python\ndef process_data(data):\n    # Directly create the \'related_io_code\' column using a dictionary lookup\n    related_io_code = _get_meta_data(data["io_code"].values[0], "related_io_codes")\n    data["related_io_code"] = data["io_code"].astype(str).map(related_io_code)\n\n    # Early return if any related_io_code is null\n    if data["related_io_code"].isnull().any():\n        return data\n\n    # Combine conditions for cleaner logic\n    mask = (\n        ((data["asset_class"] == "Local Cash") & data["location_id"].str.startswith("3"))\n        | ((data["security_code"] == "Local Cash") & data["location_id"].str.startswith("0"))\n    ) & data["related_io_code"].notnull()\n\n    # Apply transformations to matching rows\n    data = data[~mask]\n    data.loc[mask, "location_id"] = data.loc[mask, "location_id"].str.replace("^0", "3", regex=True)\n    data.loc[mask, "id"] = data.loc[mask, "id"].str.replace("^0", "3", regex=True)\n    data.loc[mask, "security_code"] = data.loc[mask, "related_io_code"] + "_" + data.loc[mask, "security_code"]\n\n    return data\n```\n\n**Improvements:**\n\n- **Combined conditions:** Instead of separate masks for each condition, the conditions are combined into a single `mask` for better readability and efficiency.\n- **Combined transformations:** The transformations for both conditions are grouped together to avoid redundant code.\n- **Early return:** The code now checks for null values in `related_io_code` and returns early if any are found, improving performance.\n- **Simplified null check:**  `notnull().all()` is replaced with `isnull().any()`, which is more concise and easier to understand.\n- **Consistent naming:** The variable `mask` is used consistently for all conditions.\n\nThese changes make the code more concise, readable, and efficient.',
