      'Sure, here\'s a basic HTML, CSS, and JavaScript code for a vibrant and user-friendly photo gallery webpage:\n\n```html\n<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang="en">\n<head>\n  <meta charset="UTF-8">\n  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">\n  <title>Photo Gallery</title>\n  <style>\n    /* CSS Styles */\n    body {\n      font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\n      margin: 0;\n      padding: 0;\n      background-color: #f4f4f4;\n    }\n\n    .gallery {\n      display: flex;\n      flex-wrap: wrap;\n      justify-content: center;\n      padding: 20px;\n    }\n\n    .gallery img {\n      width: 300px;\n      height: 200px;\n      object-fit: cover;\n      margin: 10px;\n      border-radius: 5px;\n      box-shadow: 0 2px 5px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1);\n      transition: transform 0.3s ease-in-out;\n    }\n\n    .gallery img:hover {\n      transform: scale(1.05);\n    }\n\n    .upload-container {\n      display: flex;\n      justify-content: center;\n      margin-top: 20px;\n    }\n\n    .upload-container input[type="file"] {\n      display: none;\n    }\n\n    .upload-container label {\n      background-color: #4CAF50;\n      color: white;\n      padding: 10px 20px;\n      border-radius: 5px;\n      cursor: pointer;\n      transition: background-color 0.3s ease-in-out;\n    }\n\n    .upload-container label:hover {\n      background-color: #45a049;\n    }\n  </style>\n</head>\n<body>\n  <div class="gallery" id="gallery">\n    <!-- Images will be dynamically added here -->\n  </div>\n\n  <div class="upload-container">\n    <label for="file-input">Upload Photo</label>\n    <input type="file" id="file-input" accept="image/*" onchange="uploadPhoto(event)">\n  </div>\n\n  <script>\n    // JavaScript code\n    const gallery = document.getElementById(\'gallery\');\n\n    function uploadPhoto(event) {\n      const file = event.target.files[0];\n      if (file) {\n        const img = document.createElement(\'img\');\n        img.src = URL.createObjectURL(file);\n        gallery.appendChild(img);\n      }\n    }\n  </script>\n</body>\n</html>\n```\n\nThis code provides a basic structure for a photo gallery webpage with the following features:\n\n1. **Responsive and Visually Appealing Design**: The CSS styles create a clean, modern, and visually appealing layout for the photo gallery. The images are displayed in a grid with a subtle box-shadow effect and a hover animation to enhance the user experience.\n\n2. **Photo Uploading**: The webpage includes an "Upload Photo" button that allows users to select an image file from their local device. When a user selects a file, the JavaScript code creates a new `<img>` element and appends it to the gallery container.\n\n3. **Dynamic Gallery**: The JavaScript code dynamically adds the uploaded images to the gallery, providing a seamless scrolling experience for the user.\n\nTo use this code, simply save the HTML, CSS, and JavaScript in a single file (e.g., `index.html`) and open it in a web browser. Users can then click the "Upload Photo" button to select and upload their images, which will be displayed in the gallery.\n\nYou can further enhance the design and functionality of the photo gallery by adding features such as:\n\n- Lightbox or modal functionality for viewing individual images in a larger size\n- Pagination or infinite scrolling for large collections of images\n- Sorting and filtering options for the gallery\n- Social sharing buttons for users to share their favorite photos\n- Responsive design for optimal viewing on different devices\n\nRemember to keep the code modular and maintainable as you add more features to the photo gallery.',
