      "Sure, I'd be happy to help you with that! Here's a step-by-step process to create the online coding web application using React, TypeScript, Nest.js, and MongoDB:\n\n1. **Setup the project structure:**\n   - Create a new directory for your project and initialize it with `npm init -y`.\n   - Install the required packages for the server and client:\n     - Server: `npm install --save @nestjs/common @nestjs/core @nestjs/platform-express @nestjs/mongoose mongoose @nestjs/websockets socket.io`\n     - Client: `npm install --save react react-dom react-router-dom typescript @types/react @types/react-dom @types/react-router-dom highlight.js`\n   - Create separate directories for the server and client code.\n\n2. **Create the server (Nest.js):**\n   - Create a new Nest.js application using `nest new server`.\n   - Create a `CodeBlock` schema and model using Mongoose.\n   - Create a `CodeBlocks` module with a controller and service to handle CRUD operations for code blocks.\n   - Implement WebSockets using Nest.js's built-in support for Socket.IO. Create a `CodeBlockGateway` to handle real-time updates.\n   - Expose an API endpoint to fetch code blocks and their solutions.\n\n3. **Create the client (React):**\n   - Create a new React application using `npx create-react-app client --template typescript`.\n   - Implement the Lobby page with a list of code blocks fetched from the server.\n   - Implement the Code Block page with real-time updates using Socket.IO. Use `highlight.js` for syntax highlighting.\n   - Implement the mentor and student views based on the user's role.\n   - Implement the bonus feature by comparing the student's code with the solution and displaying a smiley face when they match.\n\n4. **Deploy the application:**\n   - Build the client application using `npm run build`.\n   - Serve the built client application from the Nest.js server by adding a static assets directory.\n   - Deploy the application to a hosting service like Heroku, Vercel, or Netlify.\n\nHere's a high-level overview of the file structure:\n\n```\nproject-directory/\n|-- client/\n|   |-- src/\n|   |   |-- components/\n|   |   |-- pages/\n|   |   |   |-- Lobby.tsx\n|   |   |   |-- CodeBlock.tsx\n|   |   |-- services/\n|   |   |   |-- api.ts\n|   |   |   |-- socket.ts\n|   |   |-- App.tsx\n|   |   |-- index.tsx\n|   |-- package.json\n|   |-- tsconfig.json\n|-- server/\n|   |-- src/\n|   |   |-- code-blocks/\n|   |   |   |-- code-blocks.module.ts\n|   |   |   |-- code-blocks.controller.ts\n|   |   |   |-- code-blocks.service.ts\n|   |   |   |-- code-blocks.schema.ts\n|   |   |-- app.module.ts\n|   |   |-- main.ts\n|   |-- package.json\n|   |-- tsconfig.json\n|-- package.json\n```\n\nRemember to add clear comments and follow best practices throughout the development process. Good luck with your home task!",
