      "To find the root of the function `f(x) = x\\*cos(x) - lnx` on the interval [1,2] using both Newton-Raphson and Regula Falsi methods, we'll first find the derivatives of the function:\n\n1. Derivative of `f(x)`:\n   `f'(x) = 1 - x\\*sin(x) - 1/x`\n\nNow, let's implement both methods:\n\n**Newton-Raphson Method:**\n\nStarting with an initial guess `x0` on the right side of the interval (2), we'll iterate until the absolute difference between the current guess and the previous guess is less than `e=10^-4`.\n\n```python\ndef newton_raphson(x0, e):\n    x1 = x0\n    while abs(x1 - x0) > e:\n        x0 = x1\n        x1 = x0 - f(x0) / f'(x0)\n    return x1\n\nx0 = 2\nx_NR = newton_raphson(x0, 1e-4)\n```\n\n**Regula Falsi Method:**\n\nWe'll start with an initial guess `x1` on the left side of the interval (1) and another guess `x2` on the right side of the interval (2). We'll iterate until the absolute difference between the function values at `x1` and `x2` is less than `e=10^-4`.\n\n```python\ndef regula_falsi(a, b, e):\n    while abs(f(a) * (b - a)) > e:\n        x = a - f(a) * (b - a) / (f(b) - f(a))\n        if f(x) * f(a) < 0:\n            b = x\n        else:\n            a = x\n    return a\n\nx1 = 1\nx2 = 2\nx_RF = regula_falsi(x1, x2, 1e-4)\n```\n\nNow, we have the approximate roots of the function using both methods:\n\n- Newton-Raphson: `x_NR`\n- Regula Falsi: `x_RF`\n\nYou can compare the results to ensure they are close enough to the actual root within the given tolerance.",
