      '```python\ndef cummulative_sum(test_list):\n    """\n    This function takes a list of tuples as input and returns the cumulative sum of all the values present in the tuples.\n\n    Args:\n        test_list (list): A list of tuples, where each tuple contains one or more integer values.\n\n    Returns:\n        int: The cumulative sum of all the values in the given tuple list.\n    """\n    total_sum = 0\n    for tup in test_list:\n        # Iterate through each tuple in the list\n        for num in tup:\n            # Iterate through each value in the tuple and add it to the total sum\n            total_sum += num\n    return total_sum\n```\n\nHere\'s how the code works:\n\n1. The function `cummulative_sum` takes a list of tuples `test_list` as input.\n2. We initialize a variable `total_sum` to keep track of the cumulative sum of all the values.\n3. We use a `for` loop to iterate through each tuple in the `test_list`.\n4. Inside the outer loop, we use another `for` loop to iterate through each value in the current tuple.\n5. For each value, we add it to the `total_sum` variable.\n6. After iterating through all the tuples and their values, we return the final `total_sum`.\n\nThe function will work for the provided example outputs, as well as any other list of tuples containing integer values.',
